2026-09-27 — K01/K01b: internal invalidation-window diagnosis, NOT closure.

The matching upstream release is https://download.qemu.org/qemu-11.1.1.tar.xz
SHA 079ffbff8a7111bbc89022107cbabf3bbfd614d5fc9d7cc675991196aca12482.
One private aarch64-softmmu build occupies 1.2 GiB including source/archive;
no installed emulator, locked contract, compiler, kernel or test disk changes.
Configure with Python 3.11, --without-default-features --enable-tcg
--enable-plugins --enable-fdt=system --disable-debug-info --disable-install-blobs
--disable-download, and the existing Homebrew dtc include/library paths.
ninja -j2 qemu-system-aarch64 builds; the final diagnostic rebuild has no warnings.
The accompanying patch applies only to this upstream release; its QEMU source
contexts retain the upstream GPL/LGPL terms. It is diagnostic, not a vendor fix.

Source mechanism: notdirty_write invalidates translated code before the guest
store. tb_invalidate_phys_range_fast unlocks the page collection before returning
to the actual store. A second vCPU can translate the old branch in this window.
QEMU's earlier lock-before-translation repair is present in this release.

The final observer uses a SINGLE atomic generation/phase word, sequentially
consistent phase transitions and acquire samples around the real instruction
fetch. It records old branch 14000003 during the same post-invalidation,
pre-completion phase of a pending 14000001 store. The plugin receives the actual
fetched instruction at the two fixed diagnostic entry addresses, not a later
reread. Both kernels produce these events and subsequently execute return-one
after publication is retired. No delay or test assertion is inserted.

Controlled results (GCC-built unchanged userspace probe on both kernels):
                                         reference       subject
Unmodified private QEMU, six modes        3 PASS/3 FAIL   3 PASS/3 FAIL
Ordered decode observer, six modes        3 PASS/3 FAIL   3 PASS/3 FAIL
Post-store invalidation, fixed address     6 PASS/0 FAIL   6 PASS/0 FAIL
Post-store invalidation, no address test   6 PASS/0 FAIL   6 PASS/0 FAIL
Independent static-key/RCU baseline        1 PASS/2 FAIL   1 PASS/2 FAIL
Independent static-key/RCU intervention    3 PASS/0 FAIL   3 PASS/0 FAIL

The address-independent intervention is ONLY a second invalidation after a
slow-path, single-page four-byte RAM store whose page contains code. It excludes
MMIO/discarded writes. It is not an all-width, atomic, fast-path, cross-page or
DMA solution; no production adoption or complete emulator-correctness claim.
The first fixed-address intervention is only a causal experiment, never a
per-source/address acceptance workaround. All candidate modes remain private.

The ordered decode run has 320192/561152 actual wrong-target witnesses; they
match the entry decode observations exactly. The fixed-address intervention
has zero wrong-target witnesses. The no-address intervention passes all modes
without loading the plugin, and independently eliminates the module's missing
pointer observations. The static-key experiment does not free/dereference the
retired object; its sources, module, rounds, assertions and limits are unchanged.

Original hotplug -> reload_loop sequence: all four baseline/intervention flights
pass both the hotplug prefix and reload_loop, with no NULL fault. This sequence
is intermittent; a baseline PASS prevents claiming its original fault repaired.
It was run on the earlier 72dde6c3... diagnostic binary below, not silently
credited to the later ordered observer. The complete 23-test suite is NOT_RUN.
K01/K01b remain OPEN: general invalidation correctness and original-fault causal
closure are still required. No historical full-run count or limit is rewritten.

